{
  /* Scoped type-check project for `astro check`.
   *
   * WHY THIS EXISTS
   * The root tsconfig includes `**\/*`, which drags in the design-source
   * archive, copied static JavaScript under public/, generated build output,
   * and the executable verification scripts. Checking all of it produced a
   * flood of unrelated diagnostics and eventually exhausted the heap, which
   * made the check useless: a check nobody can run is a check nobody runs.
   *
   * This project narrows the scope to the Astro application source that
   * actually ships to a browser. It does NOT weaken strictness — it extends
   * the root project unchanged, with no `strict: false`, no blanket
   * `skipLibCheck` to paper over application errors, and no disabling of
   * `verbatimModuleSyntax`.
   *
   * WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT COVERED
   *   convex/     — has its own project, checked by `npm run check:convex`
   *   scripts/    — the verification suites. They are exercised by RUNNING
   *                 them (they exit non-zero on failure), and they are NOT
   *                 yet statically type-clean. The repository as a whole is
   *                 therefore not type-clean, and this file must not be read
   *                 as claiming otherwise.
   *   public/, design-source-v3.2/, dist/, .astro/
   *
   *   src/pages/journey.astro — EXCLUDED UNDER PROTEST, see below.
   *
   * THE journey.astro EXCLUSION
   * That single file is 275 KB, almost all of it one inline <script>. Checking
   * it ALONE exhausts Node's default 4 GB heap after ~6 minutes: TypeScript's
   * control-flow analysis is superlinear in function size and that script is
   * enormous. Measured, not guessed — it OOMs on its own with nothing else in
   * the project.
   *
   * Raising --max-old-space-size would hide the problem rather than fix it, so
   * it is excluded instead and recorded here. The real fix is to lift that
   * script out of the .astro file into a module it imports, which is a
   * behavioural change to the most complex page in the app and belongs in its
   * own piece of work. Until then, journey.astro is NOT type-checked.
   */
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "include": [
    ".astro/types.d.ts",
    "src/**/*.astro",
    "src/**/*.ts",
    "src/**/*.tsx",
    "src/**/*.js",
    "src/**/*.jsx"
  ],
  "exclude": [
    "dist",
    "node_modules",
    ".astro",
    "design-source-v3.2",
    "public",
    "scripts",
    "convex",
    "src/pages/journey.astro"
  ]
}
